    "interpretation": "Arsenic is elevated in Fe(III)- and Mn(IV)-reducing zones, consistent with release by reductive dissolution of Fe oxyhydroxides. Fe and Mn are therefore direct indicators of the mobilising process, which is why adding a field iron kit (tier E1 -> E2) is what makes the arsenic model work."
